.TH "SPGEN-QUERY" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-query \- Generates a query module for a query element
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.query [options] <QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
A named read over the read models. One new/n that returns the query — never the results. import Ecto.Query belongs to the body that speaks query macros; a body delegating to the shared QueryBuilder needs none, and the generator does not write imports it cannot justify.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the query, its parameters and its result.
.IP \[bu] 2
For the generated (delegating) body: the read model (Read Model (./read\-model.md)) — the query names it.
.SH "What the generator does"
The module, its @moduledoc/@doc, the @spec returning Ecto.Query.t(), and the new/… head for the query's parameters. The body depends on what the model says the query is:
.PP
\fIQuery, Body\fR
.TP
\fBa collection read\fR
.br
QueryBuilder.build(query, <DomainObject>ReadModel) — complete on generation, with the two aliases it names
.TP
\fBanything else\fR
.br
the spec's 1%: a stable marker that raises, so an unimplemented query fails loudly instead of returning wrong data
.PP
A collection read is the JSON:API parameter set — filter, sort, page, fields — over the live read\-model table, and Sportipedia.Support.JSONAPI.QueryBuilder is the one implementation of that: partial case\-insensitive match per string filter, comma\-separated values as an IN, \-\-prefixed descending sorts, page[number]/page[size] or page[limit]/page[offset], and sparse fieldsets as a select. Nothing in the model is left unimplemented, so the generator ships the working body.
.PP
Which reads those are is declared, not guessed: metadata.annotations."spgen.operation" on the query, read or collection. It is optional — result.type: array answers the same question and every model written before the annotation keeps working — but a declaration that contradicts the result is reported by mix sp.check, because the two would otherwise drive different files. \-\-template overrides either.
.PP
Not this blueprint: the lookup query behind a unique\-field accessor (Queries.<DomainObject>BySlug). That one is complete — it is generated by SpGen.Blueprint.LookupQuery as a dependency of the internal API (./internal\-api.md) accessor, from the unique\-slug example (./examples/unique\-slug.md).
.SH "Left to you"
For a collection read: nothing — and if an earlier run left the marker standing here, the run reports it as Outdated with the body to write, because the merge never rewrites a line.
.PP
For every other query, the new/… body, where the generated clause raises TODO: implement <query> query (see the feature spec):
.IP \[bu] 2
filter and sort by what the spec names, within the model's parameters;
.IP \[bu] 2
return an Ecto.Query — Repo.all/Repo.one is the caller's job (public API (./public\-api.md));
.IP \[bu] 2
keep the parameter arity the model states;
.IP \[bu] 2
own your imports: the generator writes none, and the compiler checks both ways — a missing one fails, an unused one warns.
.SH Tests
In the operation test (./operation\-test.md), under describe "Query": the generator contributes a placeholder case. Replace it with the behaviour the spec states — a collection's body is generated, but its behaviour (filtering, sorting, pagination over seeded fixtures) is only proven by a test.
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/queries/<_query>.ex (new/1 over read model)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>_test.exs (placeholder test for query body)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIQUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
